== (1) ladder: per-run random round versus per-call averaged kernel ==
L=10 n=20000: Pr[unfaithful run], t* per run: 0.00250 <= L K ln2/n = 0.00347; Mbar per call: 0.00718 (proved >= 0.00563); ratio Mbar/bound = 2.07
L=20 n=160000: Pr[unfaithful run], t* per run: 0.00123 <= L K ln2/n = 0.00173; Mbar per call: 0.00646 (proved >= 0.00563); ratio Mbar/bound = 3.73
L=40 n=1280000: Pr[unfaithful run], t* per run: 0.00063 <= L K ln2/n = 0.00087; Mbar per call: 0.00650 (proved >= 0.00563); ratio Mbar/bound = 7.50
== (2) stochastic human, two-point class, K = 1 bit ==
n=8: eps=0.0625; minimax lower bound eps/2 = 0.0312 = 0.0884/sqrt(n); Bayes mixture: E TV after n answers = 0.0554, average over rounds = 0.0593 <= sqrt(ln2/(2n)) = 0.2081
